NNAAMMEE
     vvttnneett — VirtIO Ethernet driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee vvttnneett

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           if_vtnet_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vvttnneett device driver provides support for VirtIO Ethernet devices.

     If the hypervisor advertises the appropriate features, the vvttnneett driver
     supports TCP/UDP checksum offload for both transmit and receive, TCP seg‐
     mentation offload (TSO), TCP large receive offload (LRO), hardware VLAN
     tag stripping/insertion features, a multicast hash filter, as well as
     Jumbo Frames (up to 9216 bytes), which can be configured via the inter‐
     face MTU setting.  Selecting an MTU larger than 1500 bytes with the
     ifconfig(8) utility configures the adapter to receive and transmit Jumbo
     Frames.

     For more information on configuring this device, see ifconfig(8).

